      "parent": "application",
      "category": "client",
      "runsIn": "browser",
      "purpose": "Select a scenario and its faults, step, play, rewind and seek through its trace, and show the step, the transitions that fired, ignored events and the claim checks of the trace so far, and the message of the step: who sent its event to whom, and whether a declared relationship carries it. A docked transport (step back, play or pause, step, the step counter and run to end) stays visible while a scenario is loaded, above the navigation on a phone and floating over the scene from 768 px, so the messages can be watched in the scene while stepping. In a panel narrower than 900 px its sections are one stack ordered for stepping: the current step (message, delivered event, fired transitions, violations), the timeline as a bounded scrolling list, the checks, then the run settings (scenario, faults, controls) with the scenario's description and behaviors collapsed under About this scenario; with no scenario loaded the scenario picker comes first. From 900 px they are three columns. From 768 px the floating transport hides while the panel itself is open. When the scenario has contract events, a Requests section lists them as a request log, one jump target per line, dimmed while still to come.",
      "implementation": {
        "status": "manual",
        "modules": [
          "src/ui/sim-panel.js",
          "src/ui/sim-transport.js"
        ],
        "notes": "Holds no semantic state; the panel and the transport drive the session's simulation functions."
      }
    },
