        "method": "data-model",
        "rules": [
          "freshness-bound",
          "holder-reaches-owner",
          "no-principal-in-shared"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "invariants-proved-within-bounds",
      "kind": "invariant",
      "statement": "A state-invariant claim reported by exegra prove as holding has a Lean theorem, accepted by Lean, that the verified explorer visited every configuration of its scenario reachable within the stated bound (over every order of simultaneous events and every subset of the scenario's faults) and found the invariant true in each; the result names the axioms the theorem depends on.",
      "rationale": "The bounded part of invariants-proved-unbounded (WG-4696). Supported by the test of exegra prove on tests/fixtures/race. The theorem is explore env inv bound maxStates = holds N; explore_sound turns it into the invariant for every reachable state within the bound. It is discharged by native_decide, so its axioms include one that trusts the compiled code, and the result lists it. Exegra records the test as evidence; it does not check the proofs itself.",
      "subjects": [
        "proof-export",
        "exhaustive-explorer",
        "formal-semantics"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "tests-exercise-shipped-modules",
        "recorded-results-reflect-current-code"
      ],
      "evaluate": {
        "method": "external-evidence"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "trace-claim-verified-needs-negative",
      "kind": "invariant",
      "statement": "A trace claim is reported verified only when it holds on every listed scenario and each of its declared negatives, of which there is at least one, violates it. A claim with no negative, or with a negative that holds or does not finish, is inconclusive.",
      "rationale": "A trace check that nothing can make fail checks how the model was written, not the design. A negative shows the claim can fail: the same script with the protection removed by a fault produces a violation.",
      "subjects": [
        "claim-evaluator",
        "claim-method-registry"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "tests-exercise-shipped-modules",
        "recorded-results-reflect-current-code"
      ],
      "evaluate": {
        "method": "external-evidence"
      }
    },
