      "evaluate": {
        "method": "external-evidence"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "pool-classes-protect-move-db-leg-under-flood",
      "kind": "measured",
      "statement": "On the pool fixture (a 20-connection pool with classes money, moves and page-reads, in front of 4 shared database I/O channels; moves at 400/s; a page-read flood of 5,000/s over 10,000 clients from 20 s to 60 s), the p99 of the modelled database leg of a move over the flood window is at most 30 ms, an assumed share of K-32's 250 ms, in at least 95% of runs at 95% confidence over 59 runs, in the base scenario and in its control without the flood; it fails in each of its two negative twins, and each twin fault leaves the control holding.",
      "rationale": "Fixture specified in docs/simulation.md, Fixtures (database pool with classes under a page-read flood), with base, control and twins; planned (WG-4715). Parameters are tagged assumed or to be measured; a holding result is model-holds, never supported. The model covers only the database leg (pool wait and I/O); network legs, host processing and replication are not modelled, so this is not a K-32 check. Negative twins: collapse-classes on the pool, and set-class-limit page-reads 12 (moves keep their reserved connections but queue behind page reads on the shared I/O channels): both must fail at 95% confidence, the second showing that class reservation does not isolate downstream shared resources; both must hold in the control. Not evaluated until recorded evidence exists.",
      "subjects": [
        "metric-claims",
        "resource-model",
        "workload-model",
        "performance-metrics"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "tests-exercise-shipped-modules",
        "recorded-results-reflect-current-code",
        "seeded-streams-independent"
      ],
      "evaluate": {
        "method": "external-evidence"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "response-time-counts-failures-as-unbounded",
      "kind": "invariant",
      "statement": "In every response-time distribution, a measured request that ended refused, timeout or error (a lost start included, by the request lifecycle), or is censored, counts as +infinity, so only ok requests are finite and a mean over a class with any such request is undefined; a claim restricted to outcomes ok reports how many requests it left out.",
      "rationale": "Planned (WG-4715; specified in docs/simulation.md, Measured outputs). Negative twin: in the pool fixture's collapse-classes twin most moves are refused quickly; a metrics implementation that took their short end - start as samples would make the twin pass, and the test must fail on such a mutant. Not evaluated until recorded evidence exists.",
      "subjects": [
        "performance-metrics",
        "metric-claims"
      ],
