    {
      "id": "metric-claims-calibrated-or-unvalidated",
      "kind": "invariant",
      "statement": "A metric claim reads unvalidated when it names no calibration, when a calibration fails on its hold-out load runs (distinct from the fitting runs, with equal workload, capacities and window; the sign-test interval of the model median over at least 6 kept runs, with no truncated run, outside the measurement band widened over repeats), when its evidence has expired at the asOf date recorded in the result or is bound to another component revision, or when a calibration tolerance exceeds the margin computed from the beta-quantile of the per-run statistic; it is flagged extrapolated outside the convex hull of the tested points with the same fault set, decided in exact rational arithmetic; and its result lists first the assumed and to-be-measured parameters, and pairs of flagged parameters, whose variation over their declared ranges flips the verdict.",
      "rationale": "Planned (WG-4715; specified in docs/simulation.md, Calibration and sensitivity). Negative twin: a calibration whose hold-out run is also its fitting run must be refused; a hold-out run whose measured p99 is twice the model's must fail and leave the claim unvalidated; a calibration with 10% tolerance on a claim with a 5% margin must not validate it; a fixture whose verdict flips when the page-read class limit is doubled must list that parameter. Not evaluated until recorded evidence exists.",
      "subjects": [
        "metric-claims",
        "performance-metrics"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "tests-exercise-shipped-modules",
        "recorded-results-reflect-current-code"
      ],
      "evaluate": {
        "method": "external-evidence"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "crash-instance-loses-state",
      "kind": "invariant",
      "statement": "A crash-instance fault stops exactly the named instance at its time: its incarnation is incremented, its timers removed, its waiting requests removed with their timeouts, its in-service requests ended with their service-done entries and its units released, its restart drawn, its notify event broadcast; every targeted entry created for the old incarnation, a reply to a call it made before the crash included, is dropped as stale; a routed entry decided for it is ignored by that behavior only, and a broadcast skips it; instance aggregates exclude it while it is down; round-robin, random, any and least-busy routes skip it; a restart edge restores only its own incarnation; a crash of a missing or already down instance does nothing; and on restart the instance is in its initial state with its initial variables.",
      "rationale": "Planned (WG-4715, defined once here for WG-4704's crash-restart; specified in docs/simulation.md, Faults in format 2). Negative twin: client C calls server S, C crashes and restarts, S replies: the reply must be dropped as stale; two overlapping crashes of one instance must not restart it at the first restart edge; engine mutants that deliver the reply to the new incarnation, restart early, or route to a down instance because it holds nothing fail it. Not evaluated until recorded evidence exists.",
      "subjects": [
        "resource-model",
        "simulation-engine",
        "formal-semantics"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "tests-exercise-shipped-modules",
        "recorded-results-reflect-current-code"
      ],
      "evaluate": {
        "method": "external-evidence"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "distribution-lowering-bit-exact",
      "kind": "invariant",
      "statement": "simulationInput lowers distributions with integer arithmetic only: the exponential and normal quantile tables are produced by the integer algorithms of docs/simulation.md and equal the correctly rounded values at the 1,045 grid points, their canonical text hashing to SHA-256 a23cd2a9566c106701375d5cf75ef982b8db6f3e52c199c47e6239649c840950; exp_fp, ln_fp and the exponential, log-normal and empirical constructions reproduce every reference output bit for bit; and a lowered value of 2^53 base units or more, a sigma above 8 or a p99 above 10^6 times the median is refused.",
      "rationale": "Planned (WG-4715; specified in docs/simulation.md, Lowering distributions). Negative twin: an implementation that evaluates the log-normal quantile with Math.exp or AS 241 in doubles, rounds sigma instead of flooring it, or computes the normal CDF at 2^-96 instead of 2^-192, must fail the table hash or a reference output; a log-normal of median 1 ms and sigma 9 must be refused. Not evaluated until recorded evidence exists.",
      "subjects": [
        "workload-model",
        "simulation-contract"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "tests-exercise-shipped-modules",
        "recorded-results-reflect-current-code"
      ],
      "evaluate": {
